.TH "LANGUAGEMODEL.CONTEXTOVERFLOW_EVENT" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LanguageModel.contextoverflow_event \- LanguageModel: contextoverflow
event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]contextoverflow\f[B]\f[R] event fires on a
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] instance when a call to \f[CR]prompt()\f[R],
\f[CR]promptStreaming()\f[R], or \f[CR]append()\f[R] causes the
session\(cqs \f[CR]contextUsage\f[R] to exceed the
\f[CR]contextWindow\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqcontextoverflow\(dq, (event) => {})

oncontextoverflow = (event) => {}
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Reacting to a context overflow
The code below shows two methods of creating an event listener for the
\f[CR]contextoverflow\f[R] event.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();

session.addEventListener(\(dqcontextoverflow\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.warn(\(dqContext overflow detected.\(dq);
});
.EE
.PP
Alternatively:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();

session.oncontextoverflow = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.warn(
    \(dqThe session\(aqs context window is full. \(dq +
      \(dqConsider cloning the session or starting a new one.\(dq,
  );
};
.EE
.SS Resetting the session on overflow
The following example creates a new session when the
\f[CR]contextoverflow\f[R] event is triggered.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]let\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create({
  initialPrompts: [{ role: \(dqsystem\(dq, content: \(dqYou are a helpful assistant.\(dq }],
});

session.addEventListener(\(dqcontextoverflow\(dq, \f[B]async\f[R] () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(dqContext full \(em creating a fresh session.\(dq);
  session.destroy();
  session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create({
    initialPrompts: [
      { role: \(dqsystem\(dq, content: \(dqYou are a helpful assistant.\(dq },
    ],
  });
});

\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] chat(userMessage) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] response = \f[B]await\f[R] session.prompt(userMessage);
  \f[B]return\f[R] response;
}
.EE
